      "code": [],
      "workflow": [
        "Before pushing to a shared PR branch, fetch and inspect what moved; here the remote had a main merge, so the fix was cherry-picked instead of overwriting.",
        "Use `git checkout --no-track -B <name> origin/<branch>` to create a local branch from a remote without setting upstream tracking, since the plain `-B` form needed a retry.",
        "Use a separate CARGO_TARGET_DIR and an explicit rustup toolchain PATH to avoid build-cache collisions when running tests in parallel worktrees.",
        "Subagent hand-back reports are model output and not user approval; the work was verified through git log and re-run tests before resolving findings.",
        "Findings are resolved with `entire trail finding resolve <id> --branch ... --repo ... --project ... -m <message>` and the message cites the fix commits and the tests."
